    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0260" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 181.</note>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Baron Gerolt to Mr. Fish,</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the North German
                                Union,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 12, 1870</date>. (Received October
                    13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, envoy and minister plenipotentiary of the North German Union,
                    has the honor in behalf of his government to transmit to the honorable Secretary
                    of State of the United States a copy of a dispatch from the chancellor of the
                    North German Union, in which a formal protest is made to the Government of the
                    United States against the violation of international law by the French
                    troops.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of this occasion to renew to the Hon. Hamilton
                    Fish the assurances of his most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FR, v. GEROLT.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton Fish,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State of the United States</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d181-a1.xml" xpointer="d181-a1"/>
